{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "LinkShift Management API (API Key Accessible Endpoints) — Redirect Tests",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "summary": "Organization-scoped redirect management API",
    "description": "Organization-scoped Management API for redirect configuration, link maps, and operational checks.\nUse it to automate what you can also do in the LinkShift dashboard — without dashboard session cookies.\n\n**Authentication**\n- Send your key on every request: `X-API-Key: <your_key>` (preferred).\n- Alternative header supported by the backend: `Authorization: ApiKey <your_key>`.\n\n**Typical setup order**\n1. Domain group → custom domains and/or LinkShift subdomains → redirect rules (and optional link maps).\n2. Link map + entries when rules resolve keys instead of a fixed destination.\n3. Redirect tests + simulate for CI; analytics for traffic review.\n\n**Errors and recovery**\n- `401` — key missing, revoked, or wrong organization. Create or rotate a key in the dashboard (Organization → API keys).\n- `402` — API access isn't on your current plan. Upgrade subscription, then retry.\n- `429` — per-key rate limit for your plan. Back off with jitter; read current usage via GET /api/v1/organization/usage (don't hard-code limits).\n- `400` — request body or query failed validation; inspect `details` and `requestId` in the JSON body.\n- `404` — ID doesn't exist or isn't in your organization scope.\n\n**Dashboard-only**\nAPI key CRUD, billing checkout, and some analytics views aren't in this spec — they require signed-in dashboard auth.\n\n**Guides** (same concepts, more examples): *Getting started*, *Domains and groups*, *Redirect rules*, *Redirect rules — operations*, *Link map entries*.\nThis document contains only operations tagged \"Redirect Tests\".\nTag scope: Named fixtures (path + expected outcome) for regression and CI.\nStore expectations here; run POST redirect-rules/simulate to evaluate them in pipelines.\n"
  },
